From 764e327dbda5045a4e75a56c7e56fa1c47faf69d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dineshr93 <dineshr93@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 06:43:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Add --sbom_output to write a protobom SBOM after the build

Builds a protobom Document from the configured targets reachable from the
requested targets and writes it as protobuf binary. Nodes carry the canonical
label as id, the target name, and the bzlmod module version when the target
belongs to a module; supplier, license and hash are omitted because Bazel
does not model them. Output is deterministic: nodes sorted by id, edges by
(from, to), roots sorted by id, timestamp honors SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH.

Uses com.google.protobuf.CodedOutputStream, already linked into the commands
target, so no new dependency and no new .proto is added.
